# /etc/thinkpad-fan-control/daemon.env — docs/CONTRACT.md §2 (example).
#
# install.sh writes the real file (existing values are preserved): exactly
# these six keys in this order.  It is read by the systemd unit through
# EnvironmentFile= and by ryzenadj-set-tdp.sh with `set -a; . file`, so it
# must mean the same thing to both parsers: one KEY=VALUE per line, values
# unquoted unless they contain whitespace or shell metacharacters (then in
# double quotes), no expansions.
#
# Who the GUI runs as.  The daemon chowns its control socket to
# FANCTL_GUI_GID, accepts socket peers whose SO_PEERCRED uid is 0 or
# FANCTL_GUI_UID, and plays the critical alert as that uid/gid in that
# session (HOME / XDG_RUNTIME_DIR) without sudo.  These live in this
# root-owned file, never in the GUI-writable config.json.  Daemon defaults
# when a key is missing: uid/gid 1000, home /home/<name of uid>, runtime dir
# /run/user/<uid>.
FANCTL_GUI_UID=1000
FANCTL_GUI_GID=1000
FANCTL_GUI_HOME=/home/jhnlstrlclcn
FANCTL_GUI_RUNTIME_DIR=/run/user/1000
# Root-side TDP ceilings (watts) enforced by ryzenadj-set-tdp.sh: nothing
# above FANCTL_TDP_MAX, and nothing above FANCTL_TDP_MAX_VRM_UNLOCKED while
# the VRM current limits are unlocked (the 30 W + unlocked-VRM configuration
# preceded the 2026-09-15 GPU hang).
FANCTL_TDP_MAX=35
FANCTL_TDP_MAX_VRM_UNLOCKED=30
